81 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 57 0 R
/E (Booking train tickets manually has always been a tedious and error-prone process. Passengers often face long queues at railway stations, difficulty in knowing seat availability, and problems when trying to cancel or change tickets. Railway staff also spend a lot of time managing bookings, maintaining passenger records, and updating seat availability.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
82 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 57 0 R
/E (A Train Reservation System \(TRS\) is designed to automate this entire process. It provides a user-friendly interface for passengers to book, cancel, and check tickets, while railway authorities can efficiently manage trains, schedules, and passenger records. By digitizing ticket booking, the system reduces manual errors, saves time, and improves customer satisfaction.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
